# HTML games — V1.0 now, V1.5 COMPILE live, V2.0 ISA later

Words: [README.md — Words used](../../README.md#words-used-in-this-project).
This is **copy 1** of Version 1.0 walls / Version 1.5 console + popular JS /
Version 2.0 machine work (copy 2:
[docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md](../../docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md)
§ Version 1.0, 1.5, and 2.0). How to write a title (FAST draw, `jmr:spr`
literals, dest on-glass) is **one** page, not a two-copy pair:
[docs/GAME_DESIGN.md](../../docs/GAME_DESIGN.md).

**V1.0** = PYTHON + FPGA-SIM + BOARD all play from `card.img`. Host mint at
card-create still works (`make_sd_image.py create` mints `NAME.JSH`). Do not
host-compile `storage/` on `RUN` as a second path.
**V1.5 compile is live:** `LOAD` → `EDIT` → **`COMPILE`** → `RUN`. `RUN`
still loads `.JSH` from the card. Compiler/editor are ordinary card programs
(`EDITOR.JSH`, `ARTSCAN.JSH`, `COMPILER.JSH`), not a new ISA. **Do not
delete** `storage/EDITOR.HTML`, `ARTSCAN.HTML`, `COMPILER.HTML` (`DIR`
hides them). Typed-at-READY
numbered authoring of *new* programs is still leftover. Popular JS V1.0 does
not have (`shift`, `Math.sin`/`round`, …) is still the language backlog
(stdlib + globals; not Canvas gradients / mouse).
**V2.0** = grow the ISA past V1 walls (sprite descriptors, ASET size,
`Object.keys`, `Math.round`, dotted `new`, `.call`/`.apply`). **No title
is the V2 example.** Do **not** title-gate (`if (stem == "…")`).

## V1.0 — write titles inside these walls

| Cap / hole | Author around it |
|---|---|
| **`MAX_SPR` = 16** ASET descriptors | ≤16 **PNG sheets** (`jmr:spr:N`). Pack frames into **atlases**; crop with **9-arg `drawImage`**. Do not ship one URI per frame (MKPVP: 274 → refuse). Keep sheets **modest** (not one multi-thousand-pixel-wide image — extra address math + SRAM traffic). |
| **`Object.keys` / `for…in`** | Compiler lowers `for (k in obj)` → `Object.keys`. RTL lacks that native (`fault=5` / `fsite=4183`). Use literal key lists or indexed loops. |
| **`setTransform(-1, …)` mirror** | PYTHON `_xf` does `max(1, w*sx)` — negative scale → 1px. Prefer **left + right** sheets. |
| **Math** | Only `floor` / `abs` / `min` / `max` / `random` / `sqrt` (+ `Math.PI`). No `round` native in V1. |
| **Heap caps (live silicon)** | `MAX_OBJ=960`, arrays `1536×32 + 12×128`, `ENV_DEPTH=384`, `ARR_CAP=128`. Loud overflow. Do not assume old 1024/512. Reuse one mutable `{x,y}` across frames — a fresh literal every tick burns the pool. Do **not** hoist per-frame grids to startup. A map bigger than 128 cells is **row arrays** (20×18 → 18 arrays of 20), not one 360-slot array — do **not** shrink the playfield to dodge the cap. [FPGA_FIT.md](../../docs/FPGA_FIT.md). |
| **16 locals per function** (`ENV_SLOTS`) | Params + every `var`/`let`/`const` in that function. The 17th is a **card-mint `CompileError`**: `LOAD` still shows the HTML, `RUN` is `?NH` / FPGA-SIM bounces to READY. Split a helper. Do **not** cut game systems to “fit 16.” |
| **No typed arrays / V1.5 stdlib** | No `Int32Array` / `Uint8Array` / `Array.shift` / `charCodeAt` / `performance.now`. Ordinary arrays, copy-down or an index instead of `shift`, packed digits instead of `charCodeAt`, frame counter instead of `performance.now`. Card mint skip → same `?NH` as a 17th local. |
| **No mouse port** | Machine play is keys + `joy()`. Chrome may also bind `clientX`. Do **not** make mouse the only way to place/aim — then PYTHON/FPGA-SIM/BOARD cannot play the same game. |
| **No per-tick maze flood** | Do **not** recursive BFS / `_copyMapOpen` / `Array(n).fill().map(()=>Array(m))` every actor every cell. HDMI freezes, **no ERROR**. One-step chase; door **`2` walks up**. Event-driven in-place flood on place/sell/reset is the eyes-home class — keep the maze. Split the BFS queue at `ARR_CAP=128` (e.g. 3×128 for 360 cells). Do **not** grow `ENV_DEPTH`/`CSTK`. [no-maze-flood-on-tick.mdc](no-maze-flood-on-tick.mdc). |
| **`fillText` 8×8 only** | One bitmap font (READY glyphs). `ctx.font` parses `NNpx` only — no TTF / `"Press Start 2P"`. Scale `k = max(1, round(N * sx / 8))` (cap 15). Glass-space: **8px or 16px**. World→glass shrink (DNKFAST `sx≈0.42`): **32px only on Score/Lives** (16px stays 8 glass px and vanishes). Do **not** enlarge title/pause/select. ASCII 32–126. Do not add small fonts to RTL. [GAME_DESIGN.md](../../docs/GAME_DESIGN.md). |
| **Glass / Esc** | 640×480 Canvas fill; Esc = machine BREAK. Present is **gone** (run 52) — scanout reads the draw bank; budget tearing, draw fast. |
| **Disk / compile (V1.0)** | PYTHON / FPGA-SIM / BOARD `LOAD`/`RUN` `card.img`. Host mint at card-create (`NAME.JSH`). **`LOAD` works + `RUN` is `?NH` / bounce to monitor** means mint skipped that title — `python3 tools/compile_js.py --html storage/NAME.HTML` prints the wall, then remake `card.img`. **V1.5:** `COMPILE` on the machine mints the same sidecar. |

**V1 library example:** `storage/MKBIG.HTML` / `MKBIGCPU.HTML` (atlases, L/R sheets, V1 Math).

**V1 product acceptance:** `INVADERS` / `PACMAN` / `DONKEY`.

## V1.5 — COMPILE live; typed-READY + popular JS still leftover

Not a title generation. Caps stay V1 (`MAX_SPR` = 16, 4 MB ASET, same heap).
Shipped glass: `LOAD` → `EDIT` (`EDITOR.JSH`) → **`COMPILE`** (`ARTSCAN.JSH` +
`COMPILER.JSH`) → `RUN`. `RUN` is unchanged — it loads whatever `.JSH` is
on the card. Typed-at-READY numbered authoring of *new* programs is leftover.

| Action | Glass |
|---|---|
| Type | leftover: `10 …` Enter, `20 …` Enter, … then `COMPILE` then `RUN` |
| Paste | leftover. Unnumbered paste auto-numbers by 10; numbered paste keeps numbers |
| Compile | **V1.5 live:** bare `COMPILE` verb. **V1.0:** compile when you make the card (minted `.JSH`). `RUN` always loads `.JSH`. |
| Replace | leftover: `10 body` + Enter |
| Delete | leftover: `10` + Enter (number only) — **gone**, not blank |
| Insert between | leftover: step by 10 so `15 xyz` lands between `10` and `20` |
| Edit | **V1.5 live:** bare `EDIT` launches `EDITOR.JSH`. Do **not** add `INSERT` / `DELETE` verbs — insert is an unused number (`15`); delete is `10` + Enter. V1.0 `LIST` / `DIR` / `LOAD` still view / learn |
| **Language** | Popular JS V1 walls/faults (still backlog): `Array.shift`/`every`/`includes`, `Math.round`/`sin`/`ceil`, `String.split`/`charAt`/`toUpperCase`, `isFinite`/`isNaN`/`parseInt`, `performance.now`, `cancelAnimationFrame`, `e.code`. Full table: [JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md § V1.5](../../docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md#v15--type-paste-compile-edit-html-at-ready-no-card-required). **Never:** Canvas gradients / `globalCompositeOperation` / mouse |

**Fit:** SOURCE stays in external SRAM. Do not grow SOURCE into BRAM. Language natives’ LUT cost is **TBD**. Full table: [JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md § V1.5](../../docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md#v15--type-paste-compile-edit-html-at-ready-no-card-required).

## V2.0 — grow the ISA (not a named title)

No `storage/MK.HTML` — that file is gone; do not treat a missing name as
acceptance. V2 is **machine** work. Historical sizing (2026-08-20 census of
the lost fighter HTML) still informs the caps:

| Requirement | Number / behavior |
|---|---|
| Sprite descriptors | **`MAX_SPR` = `PROGRAM_MAX_SPRITES` ≥ 518** (V1 = 16) |
| Asset bank | **V2.0 = 8 MB** (or more) simple SRAM port. ASIC: **single chip**, no fancy multi-bank access. V1 stays 4 MB. |
| Compiler | Accept dotted `new Foo.Bar(…)` (runtime construct-on-a-value) |
| Native | **`Object.keys`** (or real `for…in`) on exec64 |
| Native | **`Math.round`** |

```text
// BAD V1 — one data:image per frame past MAX_SPR=16
// GOOD V1 — atlas + 9-arg drawImage (MKBIG)
// V2 — raise the descriptor table when a title actually needs >16 sheets
```
